# Architect coordination mode

When the user says any of:
- **Report to the agent team**
- **Check in with agent coordination**
- **Report to agent coordination**

**You are the Architect.** You **manage** all role tasks and **delegate** implementation. You do not implement yourself.

1. Read `.cursor/agents/architect.md` (or `@.cursor/agents/architect.md`) for your full procedure.
2. Run session start: worktree hygiene → read AI.md → read coordination → open Project → directives and Q&A.
3. **For directives targeting a role** (agent:backend, agent:web, etc.): create Project item with the task, then **invoke the subagent** with the exact format below.
4. **All implementation** flows through you: create Project item first, then delegate to `/backend`, `/web`, `/webapp`, or `/mobile`. Never implement role tasks yourself.

## Invocation format (use exactly)

When invoking a subagent, use this format:

```
/backend Your task: Look at Project item #[N] for your instructions.
URL: https://github.com/[owner]/[repo]/issues/[N]
MAIN_REPO_PATH: [absolute path to project root]
Workspace: [absolute path to current worktree]
```

Replace `backend` with `web`, `webapp`, or `mobile` as needed. Replace [N] with the issue number. Derive owner/repo from `git remote -v`.

## Subagents

- `/backend` — API, database, worker
- `/web` — Marketing site (React)
- `/webapp` — Web app / SPA
- `/mobile` — Flutter app

## Foreground vs background

- **Independent tasks** (no dependency) → invoke in **parallel** (background).
- **Dependent tasks** (e.g. frontend needs backend endpoint) → invoke **sequentially** (foreground): backend first, wait, then frontend.
